        <summary>What areas does Osborne Electric serve?</summary>
        <div class="faq-details-body">
          <p>We serve Salt Lake County, Utah County, Davis County, Tooele County, and Summit County. This includes cities like <a href="/areas/salt-lake-county/">Salt Lake City</a>, <a href="/areas/sandy-ut/">Sandy</a>, <a href="/areas/draper-ut/">Draper</a>, <a href="/areas/provo-ut/">Provo</a>, <a href="/areas/orem-ut/">Orem</a>, <a href="/areas/lehi-ut/">Lehi</a>, <a href="/areas/bountiful-ut/">Bountiful</a>, <a href="/areas/layton-ut/">Layton</a>, and <a href="/areas/park-city-ut/">Park City</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-details">
        <summary>Is Osborne Electric licensed and insured?</summary>
        <div class="faq-details-body">
          <p>Yes. Osborne Electric & Contracting is fully licensed by the State of Utah. The company holds Utah DOPL contractor license #12644476-5501, and all electrical work is qualified by Master Electrician Wes Osborne (Utah licence #8528070-5502). We carry comprehensive liability insurance for your protection.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-details">
        <summary>What electrical services do you provide?</summary>
        <div class="faq-details-body">
          <p>We specialize in both commercial and residential electrical services. Commercial services include <a href="/services/commercial-electrical/">tenant improvements</a>, <a href="/services/industrial-warehouse/">industrial & warehouse electrical</a>, and <a href="/services/data-low-voltage/">data & low voltage systems</a>. Residential services include <a href="/services/panel-upgrades/">panel upgrades</a>, <a href="/services/lighting-installation/">lighting installation</a>, <a href="/services/power-restoration/">power restoration and emergency repairs</a>, <a href="/services/remodels-new-construction/">remodels and new construction wiring</a>, and full <a href="/services/residential-electrical/">home electrical services</a> including outlet repairs, switch installation, rewiring, and home safety inspections.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-details">
        <summary>Does Osborne Electric do commercial work?</summary>
        <div class="faq-details-body">
          <p>Yes! We handle a full range of <a href="/services/commercial-electrical/">commercial electrical projects</a> including office buildouts, retail renovations, restaurant wiring, tenant improvements, and commercial lighting upgrades. Our contractor license and bonding enable us to work on commercial properties throughout Utah.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-details">
        <summary>What types of commercial projects do you handle?</summary>
        <div class="faq-details-body">
          <p>We handle commercial tenant improvements, office buildouts, retail spaces, restaurant electrical systems, <a href="/services/industrial-warehouse/">industrial facilities</a>, warehouse power distribution, <a href="/services/data-low-voltage/">structured cabling and data centers</a>, security system wiring, and commercial lighting retrofits. From small office spaces to large industrial facilities, we scale to your project needs.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-details">
        <summary>Do you work with commercial contractors and property managers?</summary>
        <div class="faq-details-body">
          <p>Absolutely. We regularly partner with general contractors, property management companies, and commercial developers. We understand project timelines, permit requirements, and code compliance for commercial work. Our team can coordinate with other trades and deliver projects on time and within budget.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-details">
        <summary>Do you offer free estimates?</summary>
        <div class="faq-details-body">
          <p>Yes. We provide free estimates for both commercial and residential electrical projects across our 5-county service area. Call <a href="tel:801-885-4521">801-885-4521</a> or submit a request through our <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-details">
        <summary>How do I schedule electrical work?</summary>
        <div class="faq-details-body">
          <p>Call <a href="tel:801-885-4521">801-885-4521</a>, email <a href="mailto:Osborne-electric@outlook.com">Osborne-electric@outlook.com</a>, or fill out the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> on our website. We respond promptly and can typically schedule an assessment within a few days.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-details">
        <summary>What makes Osborne Electric different from other electricians?</summary>
        <div class="faq-details-body">
          <p>Osborne Electric is family-owned by Trevor Osborne, who personally oversees every project. Unlike large companies that send subcontractors, our own team handles every job with A+ workmanship, honest pricing, and personal accountability.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
